\end{figure}

## 2.2. Training Details

The model was trained for 10 epochs using the Adam optimizer with a learning rate of 0.001. The batch size was set to 64, and the input images were resized to $64 \times 64$. Data augmentation techniques such as random horizontal flipping and random rotation were applied during training to increase the diversity of the training data.

